---
import ProjectCaseStudy from '../../components/ProjectCaseStudy.astro';

const sections = [
  {
    heading: 'Overview',
    paragraphs: [
      'Nomod helps businesses accept card payments from a phone, payment link, invoice, or online store without buying a card terminal. I joined through Alfabolt, first contributing to the mobile product and then working on the web checkout and the payment systems behind it.',
    ],
  },
  {
    heading: 'The problem',
    paragraphs: [
      'As Nomod expanded across the GCC, adding payment providers improved rates and resilience but made the frontend harder to change. Provider decisions lived in UI code, card and wallet flows were duplicated, and some integrations risked bringing raw card data into Nomod’s compliance scope.',
    ],
  },
  {
    heading: 'What I did',
    points: [
      'Helped redesign checkout around backend configuration, so the frontend rendered the payment path it was given instead of inferring one from currency and provider-specific conditions.',
      'Built a shared card form with Basis Theory tokenization, allowing seven provider paths to collect payment details without Nomod handling raw card numbers.',
      'Consolidated repeated Apple Pay, Google Pay, validation, and provider form logic into reusable flows that were easier to extend and test.',
      'Built a shared 3DS charge-polling lifecycle with cancellation, request throttling, backoff, and a single source of truth for terminal payment states.',
      'Contributed to Nomod’s WooCommerce integration so merchants could bring the same payment infrastructure into their online stores.',
    ],
    image: {
      src: '/images/work/nomod-woocommerce.webp',
      alt: 'Nomod payments integration for WooCommerce stores',
      width: 1545,
      height: 501,
    },
  },
  {
    heading: 'How I worked',
    paragraphs: [
      'The checkout could not be replaced in one high-risk release. I worked closely with Nomod’s CTO and backend engineers, agreed the frontend–backend contract first, and moved providers onto the shared architecture incrementally. Integration and end-to-end tests protected each step while production traffic continued through the existing paths.',
    ],
  },
  {
    heading: 'The outcome',
    paragraphs: [
      'A growing collection of provider-specific implementations became one configurable checkout foundation. New payment providers could be introduced with substantially less frontend work, card collection remained outside Nomod’s systems, and the team gained a smaller, more legible surface to maintain as the product expanded.',
    ],
  },
];
---

<ProjectCaseStudy
  title="Nomod (YC S21)"
  description="Nomod is a payment processing app to sell anything, anywhere. The app enables businesses to circumvent the need for a card terminal by accepting card payments directly through smartphones, eliminating the need for hardware. Nomod offers a wide range of features, including compatibility with contactless card, QR code payments, handling multiple currencies, and accommodating entire teams."
  seoDescription="A case study of Fahad Imran’s engineering work on Nomod."
  logo={{
    src: '/images/nomod-logo.webp',
    alt: 'Nomod logo',
    width: 96,
    height: 96,
  }}
  image="/images/work/nomod-hero.webp"
  imageAlt="Nomod payment products across mobile and web"
  category="Payments · Fintech"
  period="2024—Present"
  role="Software Engineer"
  technologies={[
    'React',
    'TypeScript',
    'Redux Toolkit',
    'Basis Theory',
    'Apple Pay',
    'Google Pay',
    'WooCommerce',
    'Playwright',
  ]}
  sections={sections}
/>
